-- title:
--   Idelic stabiliser of an order is detected place by place
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb Q$ and let $\mathbb H=\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ be the associated quaternion algebra over $\mathbb Q$. Let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule of $\mathbb H$ which is an order in the sense of the project's predicate [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): $1\in\Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb Q$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $\mathbb H$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated over $\mathbb Z$. Let $u$ be a unit of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$, where $\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb Q$ relative to $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$. Write $\widehat\Lambda=$ [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q}^{f}$ generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every place, and for a nonzero prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ write $\Lambda_v=$ [`Submodule.localBox Λ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb H\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ generated by the $z\otimes c$ with $z\in\Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the completion at $v$. The assertion is: $u$ lies in [`Submodule.finiteIdeleStabilizer Λ`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L26), i.e. $u\cdot\widehat\Lambda=\widehat\Lambda$ as subsets under the pointwise multiplicative action, if and only if for every $v$ the image of $u$ under the map on unit groups induced by $\mathrm{id}_{\mathbb H}\otimes(\text{evaluation at }v)$ lies in [`Submodule.localBoxUnits Λ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45), that is, both that image and its inverse lie in $\Lambda_v$.
--
--   This is the standard local–global description of the idelic stabiliser of an order, $\widehat\Lambda^{\times}=\prod_v\Lambda_v^{\times}$ in the usual notation, for orders in a rational quaternion algebra. It is used throughout the adelic bookkeeping of the Čerednik–Drinfel'd tower, where Hecke and level data are manipulated idelically but Eichler-order conditions are verified one prime at a time.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_mem_finiteIdeleStabilizer_iff_forall_map_finiteAdeleEvalAt_mem_localBoxUnits.lean

import Mathlib
